{
  "program": "COCRDLIC",
  "caseId": "case07",
  "description": "DFHPF13 is a distinct AID byte from DFHPF1 - 0xC1 against 0xF1 - and app/cpy/CSSTRPFY.cpy:54-55 folds it onto CCARD-AID-PFK01, the same condition DFHPF1 sets, because CVCRD01Y declares only PFK01 through PFK12 and keys 13 to 24 have nowhere else to go. PFK01 is then not one of the four keys :371-376 accepts, so :378-380 forces ENTER and the transaction lists. A resolver that dropped the fold would leave CCARD-AID unset and reach the same screen by case06's route instead, which is why the two are pinned separately.",
